# Zap It Pest Control — URL redirects
#
# Format: <from-path>  <to-path>  <status-code>
# Order:  more specific rules ABOVE catch-alls.
# Portable format — read identically by both Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# TRAILING-SLASH TREATMENT (2026-09-04, per Zaydan email 2026-09-03):
#   Cloudflare Pages does NOT normalise trailing slash before matching
#   _redirects rules — Netlify did automatically. Google's Yoast sitemap
#   serves every legacy URL with a trailing slash, so every rule needs
#   BOTH source forms or we lose 301 coverage on the form Google has
#   already indexed.
#
#   TARGETS end with `/` to match Next.js `trailingSlash: true` canonical
#   routes and avoid a needless double-hop through Next.js's own 308.
#   Fragment targets (e.g. /#price-calculator) intentionally have no slash.
#
# RULE-BUDGET NOTE: an earlier version of this file paired every static rule
# and hit ~109 rules — CF Pages silently ignored rules beyond position ~102.
# Section 2 (pest-solutions) and Section 4 (blogs) are now expressed as splats
# so the file stays well under whatever the effective ceiling is.

